Applying fromAA after toAA returns the original element of A.

Two elements agree when they contain the same neighbourhoods. If the composite contains the set of all strings, so does the original element. A false-tagged or true-tagged tuple in the composite belongs to the original element by the forward half of toAA_mem_inj₀ or toAA_mem_inj₁. Conversely, a neighbourhood of the original element is the set of all strings or a tagged tuple, and the false and true tags belong to the composite by the reverse halves of those characterizations.
